  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.3.2 (forks 2.3.9) - on SpawnDev.SpawnJS 3.0.1. An app that references SpawnDev.SpawnJS 3.0.0 directly gets NU1605 (downgrade): move it to 3.0.1. Persist a session's compiled WebGPU shaders: ShaderArtifactSerializer.ExportCache/ImportCache (version-stamped), and a stored kernel now loads as an EARLY cache hit that skips IR construction, IR optimization and WGSL generation (an app restarting often - a browser extension's content script - skips nearly all of its kernel compiles). DelegateSpecialization kernels have a stable identity, so they persist too. WGSL generation ~40% faster (dead-variable pass, source-generated regexes). Half to float exact for subnormals on Wasm, WebGL and emulated-f16 WebGPU. Firefox: video frames copy through a canvas fallback. WebGPU batched dispatch: scalar arenas, bind-group reuse, pinned-header submit. See CHANGELOG.md.",
